WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:02.360
October, 1988.

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:07.820
SCP Foundation Agents Cyril Novak and Diana
Fischer had been dispatched to Austria’s

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:13.660
capital city, Vienna, to investigate a series
of mysterious, unexplained disappearances.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.300
The Foundation was unsure if these events
were connected, or even anomalous in nature,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.410
but they had reason to believe that something
was lurking beneath the dark streets of Vienna.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.760
A Foundation operative embedded in law enforcement
informed the organization that the authorities

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.530
were panicking, with an emphasis on withholding
information about these disappearances from

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.700
the public and the media.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.660
Novak and Fischer conducted a survey of the
city, observing the streets at night and keeping

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.370
a watchful eye on those who they deemed at-risk.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.860
It was the undesirables of society that were
disappearing in droves.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.300
Unsupervised children, vagrants, the homeless.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.530
All those that were indisposed, vulnerable,
and otherwise at risk of being forgotten by

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.100
society were potential victims.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:05.190
According to several sources, these disappearances
were taking place near access points to the

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.230
city’s subterranean infrastructure.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.670
Sewer holes, access tunnels, storm drains.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.610
Anywhere that led to the underground was a
potential risk-site.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:19.250
After a few days of standard exploration and
information gathering around Vienna, Novak

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:24.000
and Fishcer moved on to interviews with law
enforcement and public officials.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.480
Using a variety of cover stories, they managed
to pry out a deadly secret from the mouth

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.200
of the police chief.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.260
Human remains had been recovered near the
disappearance sites.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.890
The authorities opted to keep them a secret
from the public, so as to not cause any panic

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:43.180
of a crazed serial killer on the loose, or
inspire fears of something even worse lurking

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.990
the city’s underground.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:48.800
The Agents seized the three cadavers, and
alerted the Foundation that their mission

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.160
had been progressing as expected.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:56.909
The bodies were transported to Humanoid Containment
Site-282 in Graz, Austria, where they were

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:02.340
immediately examined by Dr. Felix Gärtner,
who performed an autopsy on the three corpses.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.549
If the Foundation was unsure about anomalous
involvement before, they were certain of it

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:08.549
now.

00:02:08.549 --> 00:02:13.980
The bodies were in shambles, mutilated beyond
belief and altered into an almost unrecognizable

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:14.980
state.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.961
The mere stench of them caused personnel working
with them to rush to the bathroom, and even

00:02:18.961 --> 00:02:23.620
those that could typically keep their lunch
down had a difficult time examining them.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.220
Cadaver-A was in pieces, and the cause of
death was determined to be from exsanguination,

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.010
or the extreme loss of blood.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:35.280
Cadaver-B was missing some important fleshy
components inside and out, some of which had

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.140
been removed entirely.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.270
The cause of death was presumed to be traumatic
cardiac arrest.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:43.400
The third corpse, Cadaver-C, was barely a
body.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.430
Instead, it was a collection of bones and
fluids.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:52.230
The cause of death, because of the opaque
conditions the cadaver was found in, was unknown.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:57.010
These grizzly deaths were only the start of
the Foundation’s containment of this anomaly,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.450
and are far from the worst this file has to
offer.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:06.530
This is SCP Explained, and today we’re going
to be looking at SCP-3288, a collection of

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:09.650
entities otherwise known as The Aristocrats.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:15.720
Dr. Gartner’s analysis of the cadavers came
to a single conclusion: a human could not

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:16.720
do this.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:20.319
In fact, he compared the deceased’s injuries
and conditions with the bodies of victims

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:22.050
of hyena attacks.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:27.720
All sustained injuries weren’t the result
of a blunt object, sharpened blade, or a firearm,

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.550
but instead resulted from a combination of
teeth, claws, and raw physical strength.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:37.599
The bodies had abnormally large bite marks,
approximately six times the size of adult

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:43.000
human teeth, yet closer analysis revealed
that the indentations did, in fact, coincide

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.430
with human teeth.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:50.070
Whatever did this possessed more than sixty
teeth, unevenly distributed over six distinct

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:55.040
rows, and required jaws much larger than those
of ordinary humans.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.489
There were unique patterns among these markings,
suggesting that it wasn’t a single entity

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:02.330
that ravaged these corpses, but multiple.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:06.620
There was no doubt about it, these deaths
were anomalous in nature.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:12.920
The Foundation issued a designation for the
entities responsible, SCP-3288, and deployed

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:18.739
Mobile Task Force Sigma-6 (“Hellsingers”),
a special unit trained to capture deadly anomalies

00:04:18.739 --> 00:04:23.830
in the field, to bring SCP-3288 into Foundation
custody.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.259
The operatives were tasked with patrolling
the Leopoldstadt District, the area where

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:30.240
the most disappearances had occurred.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:35.380
Secrecy, as usual, was a top priority, and
members of the Task Force took extra care

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:38.719
to conduct their operations away from the
public eye.

00:04:38.719 --> 00:04:43.400
As the purpose of this mission was to contain
the entities for further study, the operatives

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:49.689
were also ordered to refrain from lethal force,
and to target SCP-3288 with tracking darts

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.770
to prevent them from escaping.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.090
The Task Force divided up their assignments.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:58.751
Twelve operatives would patrol the district
and search for any suspicious activity, while

00:04:58.751 --> 00:05:03.560
ten others would remain watch in positions
with unrestricted views of sewer holes and

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.240
other underground access areas.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.879
For the first few hours, things were quiet.

00:05:08.879 --> 00:05:12.719
But then, two operatives stationed near the
Danube Canal made a report to the rest of

00:05:12.719 --> 00:05:13.800
the team.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.580
Someone near the Canal was screaming, not
loudly, but in a muffled, faint way.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:22.960
The operatives took initiative and ran off
to investigate the matter themselves, requesting

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.539
backup at the same time.

00:05:25.539 --> 00:05:30.199
Reinforcements arrived less than three minutes
later, but their teammates could not be found.

00:05:30.199 --> 00:05:34.990
Moments later, their bodies were discovered
by another operative, mangled beyond belief.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.740
Both operatives were killed, and alongside
them was the half-consumed corpse of a local

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:41.349
civilian as well.

00:05:41.349 --> 00:05:44.979
One operative’s body was recovered from
the canal, while the other was found after

00:05:44.979 --> 00:05:48.159
following a trail of blood and fluids into
an alleyway.

00:05:48.159 --> 00:05:52.240
But despite the loss of life, the mission
was still deemed a success.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:57.360
Before being mauled by the SCP-3288 instance,
the Task Force operative managed to shoot

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.639
the entity with a tracking bullet, a piece
of technology utilizing satellite location,

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:06.449
which allowed the rest of the team to follow
the entity into the sewers.

00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:11.110
The tracking was working perfectly, and the
entity was shown to be fleeing into Vienna’s

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:16.499
sewer system, until the signal faded somewhere
near the Hofburg, a palace constructed centuries

00:06:16.499 --> 00:06:21.830
ago that was once host to the Hapsburg Dynasty,
and presently serves as the seat of power

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.849
for the President of Austria.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:28.309
The team was confused, as the fading nature
of the signal suggested that the tracking

00:06:28.309 --> 00:06:32.960
bullet had been brought into a location far
deeper than the Viennese sewers were believed

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.129
to accommodate.

00:06:34.129 --> 00:06:38.669
The mission moved onward, into the depths
of the sewers in pursuit of SCP-3288.

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:45.289
The following day, the Task Force had assembled
a strategy for mapping and exploring the Viennese

00:06:45.289 --> 00:06:46.710
sewer system.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:51.300
Constructed in the mid 19th century, these
sewers were part of a larger network of subterranean

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:56.699
tunnels that included catacombs, abandoned
wine cellars, and underground rivers.

00:06:56.699 --> 00:07:01.539
Without proper planning and clear communication,
death could be a very real possibility, and

00:07:01.539 --> 00:07:04.969
not even one caused by SCP-3288.

00:07:04.969 --> 00:07:08.330
The task force was divided into four teams
of five.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.979
Three to investigate the sewers and one to
remain on standby.

00:07:11.979 --> 00:07:16.460
By triangulating the location of the tracked
instance, the Foundation was able to pinpoint

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.080
the general area they would need to explore.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:23.360
By blocking off certain exits and surface
access points, they hoped to minimize the

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.789
possibility of the entity’s escape or exposure
to the public.

00:07:26.789 --> 00:07:32.849
While the primary objective remained containing
an SCP-3288 instance for scientific research,

00:07:32.849 --> 00:07:36.490
lethal force was authorized to be used in
case of emergencies.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:41.349
The Foundation valued the lives of its trained
soldiers, and put them above nearly anything.

00:07:41.349 --> 00:07:46.509
Still, the authorization of lethal force spelled
impending doom for many experienced veterans

00:07:46.509 --> 00:07:47.719
of the task force.

00:07:47.719 --> 00:07:52.419
They knew all too well about what kind of
entity they were up against when the Foundation

00:07:52.419 --> 00:07:56.719
opted to skip the containment step and prioritize
getting out alive.

00:07:56.719 --> 00:08:01.559
A team of operatives reached their destination
safely but didn’t discover anything of significance

00:08:01.559 --> 00:08:06.270
during their trek through the sewers of Vienna,
at least not at first.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:10.749
After several hours of investigation, they
encountered human skeletal remains while making

00:08:10.749 --> 00:08:13.120
their way through waist deep sewage.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.909
One member of the task force pointed out a
loose brick in the wall, and then another

00:08:16.909 --> 00:08:18.740
did the same minutes later.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:23.419
Inspection of the area found a number of loose-fitting
bricks that were able to be removed with ease,

00:08:23.419 --> 00:08:25.800
as if they were put there to hide something.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.569
When the entryway was fully unearthed, it
revealed a previously unseen chamber, whose

00:08:30.569 --> 00:08:34.770
walls were engraved with the House of Habsburg’s
coat of arms.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:37.910
Operatives inside the chamber immediately
knew what they were looking at.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:42.310
A family crypt of royal bloodline, never uncovered
before.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:46.190
The forgotten atmosphere made them feel like
they were discovering a secret they were never

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.600
supposed to know.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:52.520
24 sarcophagi were found within the chamber,
and historical records of the sewers and surrounding

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:56.150
area mentioned nothing about a crypt beneath
the palace.

00:08:56.150 --> 00:09:01.080
Multiple statues were recovered from the chamber
as well, depicting veiled women with hushed

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.060
expressions, holding a finger to their lips.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:09.450
Almost as if to say that this place was a
royal secret, and trespassing had grave consequences

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.370
- get it?

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:13.650
“Grave” Consequences…No?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:21.000
Ooookay…moving on - The tombs themselves
were intricate, decorated with ornate jewelry

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.980
and various expensive embellishments, but
did not include placards, markings, or any

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:29.050
indication as to who was entombed within.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:32.820
When the operatives opened the sarcophagi,
they were disgusted.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:39.760
The skeletal remains of over 300 bodies, all
displaying severe and likely fatal birth deformities.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.530
The team was at a loss.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.610
What was the meaning of this room?

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:47.790
The entrance had been destroyed some time
ago, with stairs shattered and buried among

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:48.900
the stone.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:53.290
Near the other side of the row of tombs was
a vault door, coated in bronze and bearing

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.290
the coat of arms of the Habsburgs.

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:58.420
A seal, written in latin, was engraved beneath
the coat.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:01.590
Translated, it read: “For Purity of Blood”.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:05.550
The task force tried to pry the door open,
but it wouldn’t budge.

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:09.420
Opening it would require special equipment,
and after what they had witnessed inside the

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:14.170
sarcophagus, some members of the team were
even hesitant to continue trying.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:18.090
The team was ordered by the supervising team
to hold their location and await the arrival

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:20.430
of another team that would open the door.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:25.560
Foundation agents on the surface organized
a temporary evacuation of the Hofburg building.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.500
The team waited for backup throughout the
night.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:31.050
They made attempts to open the vault, but
to no avail.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:35.380
Once the surface had been properly evacuated
and an infiltration team arrived inside the

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:40.110
chamber to assist with the vault door, the
gate was able to be opened using oxygen-fuel

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.610
cutting torches over a period of two hours.

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:49.280
Once opened, the team was met with an ominous,
descending staircase, leading to an unknown,

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.700
dark location underneath the palace.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:56.830
An eight-man squad, heavily armed and equipped
with recording devices, ventured down the

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:57.830
staircase.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:01.630
Radio transmissions from the squad grew increasingly
faint over time.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:06.540
When they reached the estimated 65 meter mark
underground, their communications arrays were

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:07.540
barely audible.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:10.950
At the bottom of the stairwell was an ornate
foyer.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:16.240
Instead of decaying, gray stone walls and
oceans of sewage, there were marble floors,

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.990
with felted carpets and white painted walls
and ceilings.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:24.260
This chamber was found to be architecturally
identical to a certain wing of the Hofburg

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.260
Palace.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:29.440
Furthermore, the chamber was clearly built
in the 18th century, as many aesthetic choices

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:32.560
popular during that era were clearly present.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:37.030
Much like the crypt, there were sculptures
and statues, but this time there were also

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:40.490
columns, paintings, and tattered tapestries.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:43.680
Some of the operatives admiring the beauty
of the room overlooked that on every piece

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.730
of art, any and all depictions of the human
form were defaced and altered.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:53.670
The air was rancid, with operatives describing
the odor as similar to rotten meat and stale

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:54.670
sweat.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:59.040
The floor and walls were discolored with what
appeared to be dried, old blood.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:00.960
Regardless, they moved forward.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:05.680
In between the space’s equivalent of the
Hofburg Imperial Library was a laboratory,

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.470
not found in the palace above.

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:11.920
An operative collected numerous documents
related to alchemy, biology, and the occult,

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:16.970
as well as a journal of transactions, contracts,
and private writings.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:21.230
These documents were delivered to the above
personnel, and were later translated by Foundation

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:22.380
personnel.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:27.440
All along this chamber were human remains,
decomposing and strewn around the palace.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:33.350
Suddenly, a bell tolled, and the music of
a pipe organ began playing discordantly for

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.350
over three minutes.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:39.130
Operatives hid themselves and deactivated
their flashlights, some hiding behind the

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:43.450
curtains of a large opera hall and others
behind large instruments.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.910
They heard footsteps in the distance.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:49.470
Minutes later, a group of figures emerged
into the palace hall.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:55.700
The entities the Foundation had classified
as SCP-3288 were now fully visible.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:13:00.840
Their outfits were typical of the 18th century,
containing deep shades of red that contrasted

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:06.250
with their stark white skin, porcelain masquerade
masks, and powdered wigs.

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:12.940
Their bodies were monstrous, with arms dragging
across the floor, uneven faces, long fingers,

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:16.050
some possessing more than 10 of, and hunched
backs.

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:20.990
A pair of smaller instances entered behind
the hoard of the others, and one blew a rusted

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:24.990
trumpet while the other held a banner depicting
the Hapsburg’s crest.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:30.210
The trumpeter began speaking, but its words
were unintelligible, and raw, guttural moans.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:35.290
They ran out of the way, their stunted legs
causing them to trip across the floor.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:41.200
There were now over several hundred SCP-3288
instances inside the ballroom.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:45.270
Multiple operatives activated silent distress
calls, requesting backup to deal with the

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:48.170
mass of entities they would have to contain.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:53.300
The instances bowed their heads, and another
mass of footsteps were heard as a group of

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:58.780
SCP-3288 instances carried a morbidly obese
instance atop a throne.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:04.740
It wore a cape, a red veil in place of a mask,
and a crown too small for its head.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:07.620
It was evident that this was their leader.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.420
A large cauldron was presented before the
king.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:14.460
A small instance climbed atop the king’s
shoulder and lifted the entity’s veil to

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.630
speak to it.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:20.650
The cauldron was uncovered, and the king lurched
forward, grabbing the tub and pouring its

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:23.320
contents down its massive mouth.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:27.670
Some of the king’s disgusting meal spilled
from its mouth, revealing a small human child

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.190
with severe deformities.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:35.520
The SCP-3288 instances roared in applause
and began to feast, all while the cacophony

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:40.500
of noise brought on by the various instruments
inside the ballroom raged on.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:46.070
An operative hiding behind a harpsichord was
discovered by an SCP-3288 instance, and quickly

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:50.470
consumed by it in the feeding frenzy the entities
were engaged in.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:55.770
Still barely alive before being entirely digested
by the entity, the consumed task force operative

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:59.380
triggered an explosive device from within
the entity’s stomach.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:04.210
With a look of immediate uncomfort, the entity
suddenly exploded, taking out several other

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.560
nearby 3288 instances with the blast.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:11.910
The entities were distraught, and while they
were distracted, the task force lept into

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:18.390
action and rendered the remaining SCP-3288
instances not killed by the explosion unconscious

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:20.850
using devices loaded with a gas.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:26.290
As Foundation reinforcements arrived, the
surviving SCP-3288 entities were contained

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:33.020
and moved to Site-282, including the massive
king, whose body was transported using a specialized

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:34.030
crane.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:39.260
After the removal of all remaining entities,
the palace was filled with cement and reburied,

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:43.560
with the Foundation making sure that no one
would ever discover it again.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:48.140
After the King was contained, Foundation personnel
were shocked to discover that the entity could

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:49.140
speak.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:53.540
In an interview with the hulking monstrosity,
it revealed that its name was Maximillian

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:57.070
the Great, a patriarch of the House Habsburg.

00:15:57.070 --> 00:16:01.390
The entity’s eyesight was severely damaged
from centuries of living underground, and

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:06.070
the Foundation was able to get the King to
comply by shining powerful lights in its eyes.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:11.290
The entity was delusional, believing itself
still to be inside the palace, and referring

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:15.830
to the doctor as nothing more than mere meat,
which it wanted to consume.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:19.970
When the doctor was able to convince the King
that he too was noble blood, which the king

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:25.230
believed due to his unstable mental state,
the entity uttered a chilling statement:

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:30.010
“We are of the same noble blood.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:35.210
But some are more noble than others.

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:39.300
Our bloodline is pure - untainted by outsiders.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:42.220
We do not eat human.

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:43.970
We eat peasants.

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:45.720
We eat undesirables.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:49.690
We devour life undeserving of life.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.940
That is the nature of nobility.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:56.280
What else would be the point?”

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:01.210
DNA testing revealed that the king was, in
fact, descended from the House of Habsburgs,

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.430
as all SCP-3288 instances were.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:08.220
But what of the journal entries discovered
inside the palace?

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:12.639
After translation, the Foundation found that
they contained the writings of Leopold I,

00:17:12.639 --> 00:17:18.509
a Holy Roman Emperor and member of the Habsburg
house in the early 1700s.

00:17:18.509 --> 00:17:22.909
His writings detailed his desire to claim
power over the royal family, as well as his

00:17:22.909 --> 00:17:28.209
fears of an increased number of inbred, deformed
members of the Habsburg House.

00:17:28.209 --> 00:17:33.040
Leopold details meeting a woman of unknown
origin, who promised him that his family name

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:34.360
could live forever.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:39.149
She taught him arcane knowledge involving
experimentations of the flesh.

00:17:39.149 --> 00:17:44.539
Small animals, and eventually humans were
subject to Leopold’s disgusting, unholy

00:17:44.539 --> 00:17:45.539
experiments.

00:17:45.539 --> 00:17:49.249
Even his mystical teacher became disgusted
with what her tutelage had wrought.

00:17:49.249 --> 00:17:54.240
As payment, she demanded that Leopold cease
his reign, deliver his land and wealth to

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:58.409
common people, and destroy his various deeds
and titles.

00:17:58.409 --> 00:18:02.440
Leopold refused, and had the woman burned
at the stake for witchcraft.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:07.040
Eventually, Leopold’s experiments to make
his bloodline perpetual resulted in the creation

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.460
of SCP-3288.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:15.390
Years of inclusive family ties mutated over
one another, generation after generation,

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:20.929
until a horde of SCP-3288, living underneath
the palace and feasting on a diet of human

00:18:20.929 --> 00:18:22.490
meat, were created.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:28.429
For years, the surface Habsburgs catered to
SCP-3288’s depraved and disgusting needs,

00:18:28.429 --> 00:18:33.249
providing them with a slew of humans to feast
on and a lavish lifestyle akin to the one

00:18:33.249 --> 00:18:35.669
lived by the nobility above.

00:18:35.669 --> 00:18:41.179
One other document revealed to the Foundation
that there were multiple hives of SCP-3288

00:18:41.179 --> 00:18:43.010
existing throughout Europe.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:47.000
Most were discovered and neutralized, but
the original writing was heavily damaged by

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:52.169
mold, meaning that there were some locations
the Foundation was unable to uncover.

00:18:52.169 --> 00:18:58.960
Colonies of SCP-3288 instances buried underground,
snatching humans without any care.

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:03.200
Mutating their own deformities and living
horribly, unable to be stopped.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:09.619
A captured SCP-3288 instance in Germany revealed
that there was another entity, similar to

00:19:09.619 --> 00:19:12.669
the King in authority, by the name of the
Empress.

00:19:12.669 --> 00:19:16.570
It had this to say to the Foundation, upon
being contained:

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:19.220
“The meek will beget the strong.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:23.259
The doomed will beget the chosen.

00:19:23.259 --> 00:19:24.749
Don't you see?

00:19:24.749 --> 00:19:32.760
The greedy will devour the charitable and
the merciless will ravage the peaceful.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.850
We will make the world as perfect as us.

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:40.429
We will all be aristocrats in the end.

00:19:40.429 --> 00:19:44.279
And our Dynasty will never die.”

00:19:44.279 --> 00:19:52.150
Now go watch “SCP-1678 - UnLondon” and
“SCP-5545 - Mysterious Tunnels in Antarctica

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:56.189
- ABNORMALITY” for more anomalous subterranean
locations!

